{"type": "item", "run_id": "20261010T014622Z-routine", "option": "routine", "item_id": "e7f46a28622bd58dcffb5a2c", "title": "Building Reliable Data Analytics Agents: Lessons from the KDD Cup", "url": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/building-reliable-data-analytics-agents-lessons-from-the-kdd-cup/", "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog", "published": "2026-10-08T18:30:02+00:00", "is_ai": 0.99, "worthiness": 0.8375, "worthiness_confidence": 0.69, "final_score": 0.8375, "bucket": "high", "full_text": true, "content_source": "article_fetch", "text_chars": 12018, "delivered": true, "summary": "NVIDIA's KGMON team placed second in KDD Cup 2026 by building a data analytics agent around constrained tools and inspectable execution rather than model capability. The system unified structured data access through SQLite, provided schema context upfront, limited the agent to five core functions (schema, sql, write_answer, prose_helper), and logged all traces for failure analysis. Key insight: reliability comes from a well-designed harness around smaller models—normalize data access, constrain action spaces, make attempts traceable, and validate improvements before deployment.", "jev_ms": 352.2, "jev_input_tokens": 2917, "jev_cost": 0.000122514, "llm_ms": 2625.0, "llm_cost": 0.003263, "errors": []}
